<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fyodor Ushakov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Feodor Ushakov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fyodor Ushakov was a Russian admiral who never lost a battle, commanding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> in victories over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Kerch Strait</a>, Tendra and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaliakra">Kaliakra</a> in 1790–1791. In 1798–1799, allied with the Ottomans, he led a joint fleet that took the Ionian Islands from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, capturing Corfu in March 1799 and helping to create the Septinsular Republic. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a> canonised him in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fyodor-ushakov.jpg" alt="Fyodor Ushakov" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petr Nikolaevich Bazhanov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petr_Nikolaevich_Bazhanov_-_Fyodor_Fyodorovich_Ushakov,_1912.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
